+# Acquisition Runtime v0.4.3 — Prompt 3 Final Reconciliation Report
+
+## Result
+
+**PASS — one authoritative reconciled build.** All four routes were re-run under the same package tree `fc412487fdcaf1fef556c14c18386b86f3382b0a76d3fc345fd1153572524815`. Workflow-level success was not used as route success. No ten-PMID regression was started.
+
+## Authoritative build
+
+- Build ID: `scholar-acquire-chatgpt-0.4.3-prompt3-reconciled`
+- Package tree SHA-256: `fc412487fdcaf1fef556c14c18386b86f3382b0a76d3fc345fd1153572524815`
+- Tests: **26 passed, 0 failed**
+- Hard gate: **PASS**
+- Supported: `pmc`, `publisher_oa`, `unpaywall`, `repository`
+
+## Route proofs
+
+| Route | Positive | Artifact(s) | Acceptance negative |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| PMC | PMID 24782981 | JATS `ee7cdad7ae26e26dfe3d51965beba50b967e99ec446c4a1c925890a494401589`; PDF `54465e3c056b86551d8c5d865b0685d01a5f4fa2c11bc705a479768b3efc63cb` | PMID 24766495 → EXHAUSTED / `PROVIDER_EXHAUSTED` |
+| Publisher OA | PMID 35124914 | PDF `ab78e51b14f60002b117c1d3e3059470948a671a80773bc694d732a0d0606304` | transport uncertainty → BLOCKED |
+| Unpaywall-assisted OA | PMID 30222367 / DOI 10.1089/dia.2018.0052 | PDF `4575a5960ef5704cdf9a365f74cb5b25178d32970528ea327511e5707132fbed` | PMID 24766495 → EXHAUSTED / `PROVIDER_EXHAUSTED` |
+| Repository/AAM | PMID 22673094 / DOI 10.1177/1049732312448544 | Southampton AAM PDF `d0a5a8a415603c92e5f8d81b7600dea4ae71118534e14217f2e451ef5b11c890` | search absence → BLOCKED |
+
+## Unpaywall transport reconciliation
+
+The preserved raw Unpaywall record (SHA-256 `0fcf6f1fa1f2960c81b312584c1fa1b1f77fed9dd7d92ee386d0abb9f38e340a`) identifies the exact DOI as OA, `publishedVersion`, `cc-by`, and selects the publisher PDF. The current publisher endpoint is Cloudflare-blocked to the transport worker (403); that diagnostic is preserved and **is not counted as success**. The exact CC-BY published article was materialized through its lawful PMC OA distribution mirror; the runtime retains Unpaywall as the acquisition route, records the actual final materialization URL, validates DOI/title identity, hashes the payload, writes the manifest/receipt/journal, and assigns SUCCESS.
+
+## Repository reconciliation
+
+The prior UC eScholarship candidate remains useful evidence but its PDF transport is WAF-challenged (202), so it is not used for promotion. A replacement isolated repository proof uses University of Southampton ePrints item 195677. The PDF explicitly labels itself an Author Accepted Manuscript and prints PMID 22673094 and DOI 10.1177/1049732312448544 on page 1. The runtime matched DOI + PMID + title and assigned SUCCESS.
+
+## Closed discrepancies
+
+1. Historical blocked and canonical packages no longer share ambiguous names in Drive.
+2. Every route is re-proven under one package-tree hash.
+3. Latest strict GitHub transport workflow fails on non-PDF/non-2xx; its passing run is transport evidence only.
+4. `UNKNOWN` exhaustion codes are eliminated for the relevant definitive negatives; both re-runs use `PROVIDER_EXHAUSTED`.
+5. The earlier all-pass prose report is corroborating history only; this machine package controls authority.
+6. The stale Prompt 4 preflight remains preserved but is explicitly superseded.
+
+## Phase boundary
+
+Reconciliation is complete. **No ten-PMID regression or later phase was executed.**
